{
  "version": "1.0",
  "title": "Instagram System Architecture",
  "summary": "### 1. Media Upload & Processing Pipeline\n\nHandles the ingestion and storage of user-uploaded photos and videos. The client requests a pre-signed URL from the Post Service, uploads the media directly to Object Storage (S3), and then notifies the backend. The Post Service saves the metadata in a relational database and publishes a 'new post' event to Kafka to trigger asynchronous processes like feed updates.\n\n### 2. Feed Generation & Read Path\n\nFocuses on serving a user's personalized news feed. The Feed Service retrieves posts from the user's followers. A hybrid approach is used: for normal users with few followers, posts are pre-computed and pushed to a Redis cache (fan-out-on-write). For celebrities with millions of followers, posts are fetched on-demand (fan-out-on-read) and merged with the cached feed for the user.\n\n### 3. Engagement & Search Service\n\nManages user interactions (likes, comments) and search functionality. The Engagement Service asynchronously processes likes and comments via a message queue (Kafka) to update databases and caches. The Search Service uses Elasticsearch to index user profiles and posts, providing fast full-text search capabilities, with results cached in Redis for performance.",
